HCOMMANDS - Hollowdeep command overview

Syntax: hcommands
        hcommands mobile
        hcommands social

Lists practical original Mordor commands for exploration, combat, character
progression, equipment, and group communication. Also lists the Hollowdeep
chronicle commands. For original rules and restrictions use help <command>.

These additions preserve the original Mordor 3.00 classes and saved data.

The mobile guide lists existing short commands: l (look), i (inventory),
sc (score), n/s/e/w/ne/nw/se/sw/u/d (movement), k (kill), c (cast), and ?
(help). Short commands have the same costs and restrictions as their full
names. If quit asks you to wait, wait and issue quit again.

The social guide covers who, say, tell, follow, group, gtalk, lose, and emote.
Follow requires the other adventurer to be in your room. Group lists your
followers; gtalk reaches your leader and the group. Use lose with no name
to stop following, or lose <name> to remove one of your followers.

Quick views: hprofile status, hclass progress, hquest next.
